## First decision

### The river reading is uncertain. Apply the Bayesian update before choosing a gate setting.
as: choice

(x) Keep the gate partly open
( ) Close the gate at once

---

## A usable rule

Read the operating rule: when two gauges disagree, hold the gate setting and request a second reading.

### Two gauges disagree. What should you do first?
as: choice

(x) Hold the gate setting and request a second reading
( ) Move the gate based on the higher gauge alone

---

## Test a hypothesis

Open the flood model. Predict whether opening the relief channel will lower the upstream reading, change the relief setting, and compare the result with your prediction.

[Open flood model](assets/flood-model.html)
as: button

---

## Explain and discuss

Write a short explanation of why the relief channel changed the upstream reading. Then discuss your explanation with a colleague outside this course.

---

## Compare reports

Compare the two readings: gauge A shows 12 units and gauge B shows 16 units. List what further information you would request before moving the gate.
